    "# Test Case 5: Temperature Unit Parsing (C/F to Celsius)\n",
    "\n",
    "## Objective\n",
    "Standardize the Temperature column by converting all temperature values into Celsius (°C). If Fahrenheit values are present, convert them to Celsius. If values are already in Celsius, verify and retain them.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Expected Outcome\n",
    "- All temperatures are stored in Celsius.\n",
    "- Invalid values are converted to NaN.\n",
    "- Temperature data is standardized for further analysis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 303,
   "id": "a8ec550a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Before Cleaning\n",
      "0    104 F\n",
      "1     42 C\n",
      "2     95 F\n",
      "3     42 C\n",
      "4    104 F\n",
      "5     42 C\n",
      "6    104 F\n",
      "7     35 C\n",
      "8     35 C\n",
      "9     95 F\n",
      "Name: Temperature, dtype: object\n",
      "\n",
      "Data Type:\n",
      "object\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Before Cleaning\")\n",
    "print(production[\"Temperature\"].head(10))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nData Type:\")\n",
    "print(production[\"Temperature\"].dtype)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 304,
   "id": "b0568b24",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Function to convert temperature to Celsius\n",
    "def convert_to_celsius(temp):\n",
    "\n",
    "    temp = str(temp).strip().upper()\n",
    "\n",
    "    if temp.endswith(\"F\"):\n",
    "        value = float(temp.replace(\"F\", \"\").strip())\n",
    "        return round((value - 32) * 5 / 9, 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    elif temp.endswith(\"C\"):\n",
    "        value = float(temp.replace(\"C\", \"\").strip())\n",
    "        return value\n",
    "\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply conversion\n",
    "production[\"Temperature\"] = production[\"Temperature\"].apply(convert_to_celsius)"
   ]
  },
